; archema.concept-matrix.udon — scenario-corpus edition
; Pseudo-real: same genre as archema-io/charter/concept-matrix.md, recast
; as UDON — one |concept per shared idea, mapping where each program member
; carries it. Note the two-part cross-document joins (:in <file> + :ref
; <in-file reference>): the reference syntax is document-scoped, so
; pointing INTO another file takes a file attr beside the @-ref. The
; understanding scenarios probe exactly that seam.

|concept-matrix[archema]
  :charter CHARTER-DRAFT.md
  :updated <2026-07-20>

  |concept[promise]
    :status aligned
    |carrier :in vivarium.lexicon.udon :ref @term[promise]
    |carrier :in terrestris.ordinum.udon :ref @meta[reading-rules]
    A defeasible forward commitment; the lexicon defines it, the ordinum
    instantiates it per phase.

  |concept[process-health]
    :status aligned
    |carrier :in asf-processes.process-map.udon :ref @process-map[asf-processes]
    Health/drain tagging of running processes; ASF is the only carrier so
    far — vivarium's PROCESS.udon is a candidate adopter.

  |concept[decision-authority]
    :status drifting
    |carrier :in vivarium.decision-log.udon :ref @decision[claim-requires-nil]
    |carrier :in asf-processes.process-map.udon :ref @process[valve]
    The joseph/us/claude authority taxonomy vs the valve's
    "genuinely-his calls" — same idea, two vocabularies; a term-carve is
    pending.

  |concept[fidelity-ladder]
    :status single-carrier
    |carrier :in vivarium.lexicon.udon :ref @term[fidelity-ladder]
    Spend representation by consequence. ASF's abstraction-tier language
    may be the same idea wearing different clothes; unverified.
